    {
      "id": "gux0iut",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly categorized into communicable (infectious) and non-communicable (non-infectious) diseases.",
        "Communicable diseases are caused by biological pathogens including bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoans.",
        "Immunity is classified into Innate (present from birth, non-specific) and Acquired (developed after birth, pathogen-specific).",
        "Deficiency diseases occur due to prolonged lack of specific essential nutrients, vitamins, or minerals.",
        "Vaccination works by introducing inactivated or weakened antigens to stimulate antibody production and immunological memory."
      ],
      "id": "bgui71q"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xks31db",
      "content": "• A disease is a condition that impairs normal body function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "czsx5ll",
      "content": "• It may cause pain, weakness, discomfort or dysfunction of organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xjr830d",
      "content": "• Diseases may be infectious or non‑infectious."
    },
    {
      "id": "mr7whot",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Types of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vrvdkdl",
      "content": "• Communicable diseases – Spread from one person to another."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "exwt42z",
      "content": "• Non‑communicable diseases – Do not spread between individuals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sv5p0t4",
      "content": "• Deficiency diseases – Caused by lack of nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "doe6wgc",
      "content": "• Hereditary diseases – Passed through genes."
    },
    {
