      "id": "k5eh9zg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Immune System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ygeqwac",
      "content": "• The immune system protects the body from pathogens."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "21odsci",
      "content": "• It includes white blood cells, antibodies and lymphatic organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Communicable Diseases",
        "Non-Communicable Diseases"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Infectious and transmissible from one individual to another",
          "Non-infectious and cannot spread from person to person"
        ],
        [
          "Caused by external biological pathogens (bacteria, viruses, etc.)",
          "Caused by genetic, nutritional, environmental, or lifestyle factors"
        ],
        [
          "Examples: Tuberculosis, Cholera, COVID-19, Malaria",
          "Examples: Diabetes Mellitus, Scurvy, Hypertension, Cancer"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "mdovhph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eotkibg",
      "content": "• It identifies and destroys harmful microorganisms."
    },
    {
