    {
      "id": "ckcme4m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Vaccination"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mymkbkx",
      "content": "• Vaccines stimulate the immune system to produce antibodies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mbxdsvm",
      "content": "• They protect against diseases such as polio, measles and hepatitis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x24xtp6",
      "content": "• Vaccination is one of the most effective methods of disease prevention."
    },
    {
      "id": "smwcucc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Prevention of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "te3f1az",
      "content": "• Maintain personal hygiene."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bxg0zrn",
      "content": "• Eat a balanced diet."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3e1oit1",
      "content": "• Drink clean water."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Edward Jenner is known as the Father of Immunology for developing the smallpox vaccine in 1796.",
        "BCG (Bacille Calmette-Guérin) vaccine is given for Tuberculosis, while DPT protects against Diphtheria, Pertussis, and Tetanus.",
        "Malaria is caused by the protozoan Plasmodium and transmitted by female Anopheles mosquitoes.",
        "Innate immunity provides immediate, non-specific defense barriers (physical, chemical, and cellular)."
      ],
      "id": "fbkaliq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rwg0j7x",
      "content": "• Regular vaccination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "39skc7o",
      "content": "• Control insects and mosquitoes."
    },
    {
      "id": "f14fx74",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ifzvkxo",
      "content": "• Vaccines help build immunity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zyonhtm",
      "content": "• Vitamin deficiencies cause several diseases."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1qeap1q",
      "content": "• Pathogens include bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gvi8bh1",
      "content": "• The immune system defends the body against infections."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
